# Custom fields — /api/custom-fields
#
# Run `dotnet run --project JsonApiPoc` first, then click the gutter icon next to a request.
# `###` separates requests; the text after it is the request name. "->" notes the expected outcome.
#
# The tenant-defined field catalog: one resource per (resourceType, key). Clients read it to build
# dynamic forms, then read and write the values through each resource's `customFields` attribute.
#
# Seed: contacts -> leadSource (text), newsletterOptIn (boolean)
#       deals    -> probability (number), competitor (text), contractSignedDate (date)
#
# Read-only, and the only map with no SelfLink — there is no GET /api/custom-fields/{id} route
# to point at, so the resources carry no links member.

@host = http://localhost:5031

### The whole catalog
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Catalog for deals (drives a dynamic deal form)
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields?filter[resourceType]=deals
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Catalog for contacts
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields?filter[resourceType]=contacts
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Companies define no custom fields -> 200 with data: [], meta.total 0
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields?filter[resourceType]=companies
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sorted by key
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields?sort=key
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Grouped by resource type, then key
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields?sort=resourceType,key
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Filter, sort, and sparse fieldset together — just what a form builder needs
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields?filter[resourceType]=deals&sort=key&fields[custom-fields]=key,label,dataType
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Second page of 2 -> links.prev/next, meta.total
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields?page[number]=2&page[size]=2
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

# The values themselves ride along on each resource, not here:
#   GET /api/contacts/1   -> attributes.customFields = { "leadSource": "referral", ... }
#   GET /api/deals/1      -> attributes.customFields = { "probability": 60, ... }
# Values are typed on read according to this catalog's dataType.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Query validation -> 400 problem details
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Unknown resourceType filter value -> 400 (allowed values listed in detail)
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields?filter[resourceType]=gadgets
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Undeclared filter name -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields?filter[dataType]=text
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unsupported sort field -> 400 (detail lists key, resourceType)
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields?sort=label
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unknown query parameter -> 400 (strict validation)
GET {{host}}/api/custom-fields?foo=bar
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
